(:taskCollection
  :id "Phase446MultiRuntimeRelayAndObservability"
  :createdAt 1789142392680
  :status "planned"
  :priorityOrder 10
  :summary "Multi-Runtime Relay and Observability: one wire contract and one causal trace across in-browser, local, server and relay runtimes, with ownership partitioned at the relay so parallel development cannot lose work, and camelCase enforced on every emitter before the surfaces multiply."
  :phase "Phase446MultiRuntimeRelayAndObservability"
  :baseline "2026-09-11: agent-bus holds 2030 lines across fourteen modules with browser, sse, http and wasm references and fourteen test files, yet has zero inbound references from the CLI; browser-plugin and asl-bridge are currently listed for removal by Task43807; no wasm artifact exists; the boundary policy is native-only; ASN property keys are 48.5 percent camelCase with machine emitters unmigrated; this session lost work twice to unleased concurrent writers on a single machine."
  :tasks [
    (:task
      :id "Task44601"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-446"
      :title "Reclassify the relay surfaces from removal candidates to runtime targets"
      :kind :protocol
      :lane "topology"
      :state :done
      :priority :critical
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789142392680
      :updatedAt 1789438800000
      :motivation "Task43807 lists browser-plugin and asl-bridge among packages to delete because they have zero inbound references, which was the correct read when the goal was pruning. The stated goal is now cross-runtime operation across in-browser, local machine, server and agent relay, and those two packages plus agent-bus are exactly those surfaces: agent-bus alone is 2030 lines across fourteen modules (bus, mesh, cluster, presence, transport, wire, gateway, browser-bridge, tool_plane, mvcc_bus, nd_asn, proc_telemetry) with fourteen test files and declared browser, sse, http and wasm transports. Zero inbound references means unreachable, not worthless."
      :purpose "Amend Task43807 to retain agent-bus, browser-plugin, asl-bridge, asl-gateway and vdom as runtime targets with declared entry points, and record which of the thirteen packages remain removal candidates. A package is retained only when this phase gives it a reachable entry point and a gate; otherwise it returns to the removal list rather than lingering as an exception."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Retained set declared with entry points" "Removal set reduced and re-justified" "No package retained without a gate in this phase"]
      :owns [".asl/mem/tasks/Phase438LanguageOptimizationAndPortableCore.asn" ".asl/mem/components.asn"]
      :targetSymbols ["run_gate_1"]
