    (:task
      :id "Task44602"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-446"
      :title "One wire contract across runtimes: ASN frames over stdio, unix socket, http and sse"
      :kind :protocol
      :lane "transport"
      :state :done
      :priority :critical
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789142392680
      :updatedAt 1789439100000
      :motivation "The bus declares four transports and the engine speaks a fifth shape on stdout; nothing states that a frame means the same thing on each. Cross-runtime communication whose framing differs per transport reproduces, at the protocol layer, the same class of silent divergence the audits found in the gate layer."
      :purpose "One frame schema in asl/grammar/wire.asn with camelCase keys, carried identically over stdio, unix socket, http and sse: identity, sessionId, causality, payload and digest. Each transport is a codec over that schema and nothing else. A frame that fails schema validation is rejected at ingress with a typed error rather than partially processed."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Single frame schema with camelCase keys" "Four transports as codecs over it" "Ingress validation with typed rejection" "Conformance vectors shared across transports"]
      :owns ["asl/grammar/wire.asn" "agent-bus/src/wire.asl" "agent-bus/src/transport.asl" "asl/tools/asl.c"]
      :targetSymbols ["execute_single_step"]
      :relatedSymbols ["output" "tools" "names"]
      :invariants ["D34" "D51" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task44601" "Task43803"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44602"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task44602.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["The same frame round-trips identically over all four transports; a frame valid on one and invalid on another fails the conformance vectors." "A malformed frame is rejected at ingress and never partially applied."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44602" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [(:receipt :taskId "Task44602" :passed true :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44602" :assertCount 78 :at 1789439100000)]
      :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Verifier freezes frame vectors valid and invalid." "Define the schema." "Implement each transport as a codec." "Reject invalid frames at ingress." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 1
      :receipts [(:receipt :step 1 :status :ok :hash "HEAD")])
    (:task
      :id "Task44603"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-446"
      :title "Cross-runtime observability: one trace spanning browser, local, server and relay"
      :kind :protocol
      :lane "observability"
      :state :done
      :priority :critical
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789142392680
      :updatedAt 1789439300000
      :motivation "The session trace in Task44207 is per process. With work distributed across an in-browser runtime, a local engine, a server and a relay, a per-process trace cannot answer what happened, which is the question every stage of the loop depends on. Causality across runtimes is the part that cannot be reconstructed afterwards."
      :purpose "Every frame carries sessionId, parent frame digest and a monotonic sequence, so traces from separate runtimes merge into one causal order; (:trace :scope :mesh) returns the merged view; a gap in the sequence is reported as a gap rather than silently closed. Clock skew is handled by causal order, not timestamps."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Causal identity on every frame" "Merged mesh-scope trace" "Sequence gaps reported explicitly" "Clock skew does not reorder"]
      :owns ["agent-bus/src/mesh.asl" "agent-bus/src/presence.asl" "asl/tools/asl.c" ".asl/mem/telemetry"]
      :targetSymbols ["execute_single_step"]
      :relatedSymbols ["anchor" "output" "grading"]
      :invariants ["D34" "D51" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task44207" "Task44602"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44603"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task44603.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["Two runtimes producing interleaved work merge into one order that respects causality regardless of clock skew; a dropped frame appears as a reported gap, never as a silent renumbering." "The merged trace is readable by asl reflect without runtime-specific handling."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44603" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [(:receipt :taskId "Task44603" :passed true :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44603" :assertCount 80 :at 1789439300000)]
      :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Verifier fixes a two-runtime scenario with a dropped frame." "Add causal identity to frames." "Merge traces by causal order." "Report gaps." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 1
      :receipts [(:receipt :step 1 :status :ok :hash "HEAD")])
    (:task
      :id "Task44604"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-446"
      :title "Parallel development across runtimes: partitioned ownership and conflict resolution at the relay"
      :kind :protocol
      :lane "parallel"
      :state :done
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789142392680
      :updatedAt 1789439400000
      :motivation "File leases in Task44203 are local to one filesystem. Parallel development across runtimes needs the partition to hold when two agents on different machines touch the same logical artifact, and this session twice lost work to an unleased concurrent writer on a single machine."
      :purpose "The relay holds the authoritative lease table keyed by logical path and sessionId; a claim is granted by the relay, not by the local engine; a write whose lease is not current is rejected with ERR_STALE_LEASE at the relay before it reaches a filesystem; releasing is explicit and expiry fails closed. Partitions are declared per task :owns so the DAG determines who may write what."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Relay-held lease table" "Claim and release across runtimes" "ERR_STALE_LEASE at the relay" "Partitions derived from task :owns"]
      :owns ["agent-bus/src/cluster.asl" "agent-bus/src/gateway.asl" "asl/tools/asl.c"]
      :targetSymbols ["execute_single_step"]
      :relatedSymbols ["parallel" "oneStep" "hiddenTests"]
      :invariants ["D34" "D51" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task44203" "Task44602"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44604"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task44604.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["The second claimant is refused and its write never reaches a filesystem; an expired lease fails closed rather than being renewed implicitly." "Two agents working disjoint partitions proceed without contention."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44604" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [(:receipt :taskId "Task44604" :passed true :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44604" :assertCount 74 :at 1789439400000)]
      :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Verifier fixes two runtimes claiming one path." "Implement the relay lease table." "Reject stale writes at the relay." "Derive partitions from :owns." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 1
      :receipts [(:receipt :step 1 :status :ok :hash "HEAD")])
    (:task
      :id "Task44605"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-446"
      :title "In-browser runtime: wasm engine with OPFS-backed workspace and the same boundary policy"
      :kind :protocol
      :lane "browser"
      :state :done
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789142392680
      :updatedAt 1789142392680
      :motivation "Wasm engines have no native file system; boundary policies that assume POSIX paths fail in browser contexts; OPFS gives a sandboxed origin-private file system with similar tree semantics, but requires path normalization and explicit boundary verification."
      :purpose "Implement an in-browser wasm engine runner backed by OPFS, sharing the path-boundary verification logic with the native engine, and report browser capabilities cleanly."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Wasm engine runs in browser with OPFS workspace" "Same path-boundary policy applied to OPFS paths" "Missing capabilities reported cleanly with fallbacks" "Browser trace frames merge into cross-runtime mesh trace"]
      :owns ["browser-plugin/src" "agent-bus/src/browser-bridge.asl" "asl/tools/asl.c"]
      :targetSymbols ["OpfsWorkspace" "is-safe-opfs-path?" "make-browser-wasm-engine" "dispatch-browser-wasm-step" "BrowserCapability" "list-browser-capabilities" "query-browser-capability" "BrowserTraceFrame" "make-browser-trace-frame" "emit-browser-trace-frame" "query-browser-bridge-capability"]
      :relatedSymbols ["pathBoundary" "wasmBatchRpc" "runCommand" "nativeFs"]
      :invariants ["D34" "D80" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task43803" "Task43809" "Task44210"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44605"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task44605.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A path escaping the OPFS workspace is rejected by the same policy that rejects it natively; a capability unavailable in the browser reports absent with a fallback rather than failing opaquely." "The browser runtime emits frames that merge into the mesh trace."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44605" :status :passed :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [
        (:receipt :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44605" :status :passed :exitCode 0 :assertionsEvaluated 82 :timestamp 1789142392740)
      ]
      :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Verifier fixes boundary cases under OPFS." "Run the wasm engine in-browser." "Map OPFS roots into the boundary policy." "Report capability gaps." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 5
      :receipts [
        (:receipt :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44605" :status :passed :exitCode 0 :assertionsEvaluated 82 :timestamp 1789142392740)
      ])
    (:task
      :id "Task44606"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-446"
      :title "camelCase across the wire and the ledgers, enforced not asserted"
      :kind :protocol
      :lane "naming"
      :state :planned
      :priority :medium
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789142392680
      :updatedAt 1789142392680
      :motivation "Measured: ASN property keys are 48.5 percent camelCase, with the hand-authored D52 task schema converged and the machine emitters (exit-code 388 occurrences, latency-ms 225, stdout-len 169, tokens-out 150) never migrated. Those emitters are exactly the telemetry and wire surfaces this phase multiplies across four runtimes, so the divergence would be replicated rather than fixed."
      :purpose "Every emitter writing ASN uses camelCase keys: telemetry, receipts, trace frames, wire frames and bus payloads; the D51 checker from Task44503 covers emitted output as well as source, so a new emitter cannot introduce kebab-case keys."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["All emitters produce camelCase keys" "Checker covers emitted output, not only source" "Existing kebab-case telemetry keys migrated with a recorded mapping"]
      :owns ["agent-bus/src" "harness/src" "asl/tools/asl.c" ".asl/mem/telemetry"]
      :targetSymbols ["run_gate_6"]
      :relatedSymbols ["names" "output" "ssot"]
      :invariants ["D34" "D51" "D81"]
